WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.350
Across the Marvel Cinematic Universe's many
movies, countless epic fights have unfolded.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:10.160
We've seen incredible showdowns between the
likes of Thor and Hulk, Hulk and the Hulkbuster,

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.840
Captain America and Red Skull, and so many
more.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:17.201
However, for as many cool fight scenes as
there are across the MCU's filmography, it's

00:00:17.201 --> 00:00:21.650
pretty obvious that some conflicts in the
MCU are inherently more captivating than their

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:22.650
peers.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.960
These are the greatest fight scenes in the
MCU.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.160
"YES!"

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.160
Captain America vs. Iron Man

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:35.270
This fight in Captain America: Civil War is
the payoff to over half a decade's worth of

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:38.690
tension-building between the MCU's two biggest
heroes.

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:42.630
Across both Avengers movies, we'd see these
fan-favorite characters butt heads, while

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:45.510
their solo movies pushed them even farther
into different perspectives.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:50.260
That kind of friction could only be resolved
in one way, and audiences were waiting for

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:51.260
it.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:54.470
The scene let us revel in seeing our favorite
hero beat the snot out of the other guy, and

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:57.780
gave us an MCU fight with some actual emotional
stakes.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.460
Another excellent aspect of the fight is how
close it is to its comic book counterpart

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:03.780
in terms of general tone and shot composure.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:13.700
The battle pays tribute to its source material
without being limited by it, and raises the

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:18.680
MCU's cinematography standards all inside
a few short, sweet minutes.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.360
The Hydra Fortress Assault

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:24.350
Courtesy of Avengers: Age of Ultron, this
fight scene, from the moment it begins, is

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.130
an absolute joy.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:30.140
Not only does it display each of the core
Avengers in all their glory, but it does so

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:34.070
through the use of one continuous shot that
strings together the different Avengers in

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:36.570
a sweeping, interconnected style.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.460
Every Avenger gets their time to shine.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:42.560
As icing on the cake, the opening scene caps
off with a beautiful group shot of all the

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.970
Avengers leaping into battle as a combined
unit, and it's at that moment you're reminded

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:50.700
why Marvel's interconnected universe was worth
all the effort.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:56.320
[Fighting and grunting]

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.350
Iron Man's assault on terrorism

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:03.880
It's one of Iron Man's first major fight scenes,
featuring Tony Stark taking down terrorists

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:08.690
in the Middle East right after he's developed
his Mark 3 Iron Man suit, and it's an instantly

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:11.060
classic collection of cool moments.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:17.940
[Gunshots and explosions]

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:22.780
This single scene was a milestone for superhero
cinematography, displaying a whole new breed

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:27.020
of superhero action that fans at the time
didn't even know was possible.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:29.880
Iron Man and War Machine vs. Hammer drones

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:34.120
But wait, Iron Man's battles got even cooler
when Iron Man 2 came along.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:38.050
No other fight scene in the MCU's history
has filled its frames with cherry blossom

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:42.820
petals swirling around two guys in robot suits,
and that can only be considered a huge missed

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:45.599
opportunity given how cool it looked in this
scene.

00:02:45.599 --> 00:02:49.170
More importantly, this scene is one of the
only times we get to see Rhodey use his War

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.050
Machine armor to its fullest potential.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:56.450
While he and Iron Man get a cool team-up throwback
scene in Age of Ultron, nothing quite compares

00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:01.790
to their first go-around at the end of Iron
Man 2.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:07.480
"I think you should lead with that next time."

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.640
The Guardians of the Galaxy vs. Ronan

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:13.650
Towards the end of Guardians of the Galaxy,
Ronan the Accuser saddles up to declare his

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:17.940
triumph over the Nova Corps and the Guardians,
until Star-Lord interrupts him and challenges

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:20.200
him to a fight to the death… by dance-off.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:24.130
[Singing] "Oooh, child, things are gonna get
easier.

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:27.590
Ooooh, child, things will get brighter.

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:29.620
Listen to these words."

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:32.000
What comes after, however, might be even better.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.410
The Guardians, united, join forces in the
most unironically epic hand-holding session

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:41.110
in the history of cinema, literally vaporizing
Ronan with his own infinity stone.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:44.290
If only all dance-offs ended this way.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.909
The tarmac throwdown

00:03:45.909 --> 00:03:50.560
So far, not one other movie in the massive,
multi-franchise saga can claim to have a scene

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:55.239
with as much raw, literal superheroism as
this one from Civil War, given that there

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:59.600
are no fewer than twelve Marvel superheroes
throwing down at the same time.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:08.060
[When all your friends start having a political discussion.]

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:12.370
Civil War's tarmac scene is a cacophony of
comic book noise crammed into frames that

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:14.750
are barely big enough to hold all the action.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:19.810
For the sheer scope of the fight alone, this
scene easily earns its slot on this list.

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:22.039
Captain America and Bucky's final fight

00:04:22.039 --> 00:04:26.210
There's not a single fight in the MCU's history
that's quite as painful to watch as the one

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:30.009
between Bucky and Cap at the end of Captain
America: The Winter Soldier.

00:04:30.009 --> 00:04:34.199
Not only are the stakes ridiculously high,
but they're also intensely personal.

00:04:34.199 --> 00:04:38.520
The only person keeping Cap from saving the
lives of millions is Bucky Barnes, Cap's longtime

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:39.809
best friend.

00:04:39.809 --> 00:04:40.809
"Bucky?"

00:04:40.809 --> 00:04:44.729
"Who the hell is Bucky?"

00:04:44.729 --> 00:04:48.849
It's absolutely heartbreaking to watch Bucky
attack Cap, knifing him and smashing his body

00:04:48.849 --> 00:04:53.340
to a pulp as the latter desperately tries
to deactivate the helicarrier and save innocent

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.340
lives.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:59.130
There are more action packed scenes in the
MCU, but none as intensely personal and character-driven

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:00.370
as this one.

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:01.360
"Bucky.

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:07.080
You've known me your whole life."

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:08.819
Ultron crashes the party

00:05:08.819 --> 00:05:13.070
While this battle from Age of Ultron is nowhere
close to being the most bombastic fight scene

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:17.449
in the MCU, it's great for a whole different
reason: without a doubt, it's the coolest

00:05:17.449 --> 00:05:20.189
entrance of a villain in the MCU's history
to date.

00:05:20.189 --> 00:05:24.430
Ultron says some harrowing words before siccing
a bunch of hijacked Iron Legion troops on

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:26.759
the Avengers in their own meeting room.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:28.200
"Peace in our time."

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:34.689
From there, caught with their pants down,
all the Avengers scramble to defend themselves.

00:05:34.689 --> 00:05:38.740
Instead of Iron Man just pointing his hand
at things or Hulk smashing, the Avengers actually

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:43.650
need to display some slick moves and dodge
attacks with acrobatic finesse.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:44.650
The Incident

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:48.419
You'd be hard-pressed to find a soul alive
that wouldn't qualify the Battle of New York,

00:05:48.419 --> 00:05:53.039
aka The Incident, as one of the Marvel Cinematic
Universe's greatest fights.

00:05:53.039 --> 00:05:57.990
From top to bottom, this enormous battle from
The Avengers an absolute behemoth: it's nearly

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:02.779
40 minutes of Iron Man, Captain America, Hulk,
Thor, Black Widow and Hawkeye smashing the

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:07.060
ever-living crap out of Chitauri warriors,
in increasingly impressive ways.

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:14.100
[Roaring]

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:19.880
Before you know it, Iron Man is bouncing his
repulsor beams off Cap's shield to wipe out

00:06:19.889 --> 00:06:22.569
entire conga lines of bad guys in a single
blow.

00:06:22.569 --> 00:06:28.039
Hulk is guarding Thor while he summons lightning
bolts directly into massive alien slugs' spines.

00:06:28.039 --> 00:06:33.060
Hawkeye uses otherworldly archery skills while
Black Widow pilots a flying hoverbike.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:35.659
It's a legendary scene from start to finish.

00:06:35.659 --> 00:06:38.470
The actual greatest fight in the MCU

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:42.580
As great as the Avengers' throwdown in New
York was, let's not pretend its glory came

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:45.729
from heroes like Iron Man, Captain America,
or Black Widow.

00:06:45.729 --> 00:06:49.569
These characters were all fine, sure, and
we paid them their due above, simply because

00:06:49.569 --> 00:06:53.819
it would've been rude to do otherwise before
we arrived at the real champions.

00:06:53.819 --> 00:06:58.689
These two mystery contenders and their absolutely
glorious brawl have, and will, reign supreme

00:06:58.689 --> 00:07:04.809
over all other MCU fight scenes today, yesterday,
and tomorrow, and it's highly unlikely The

00:07:04.809 --> 00:07:07.439
Avengers: Infinity War will feature anything
better.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:08.440
We present to you:

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:14.640
[Punch]

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:17.659
It's short, sweet, and absolutely brutal.

00:07:17.659 --> 00:07:21.250
Brutal enough to oust every other fight on
this list from their shot at being number

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:22.250
one.

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:25.509
Thanos has no clue what he's about to go up
against.

00:07:25.509 --> 00:07:26.509
Thanks for watching!

00:07:26.509 --> 00:07:28.770
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:30.939
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

